+# BLUE CURRENT V48.30.0 — V48 RELEASE CLOSURE & CERTIFICATION
+
+V48 is complete.
+
+## V48 commercial proof chain
+BASELINE → PROVE → REVIEW → DECIDE → PLAN
+
+The final certification surface aggregates the complete V48 chain without mutating pilot data.
+
+### Certification contracts
+1. Pilot value baseline exists.
+2. Proof program is active.
+3. Executive review packet exists.
+4. Human-decision boundary prevents automatic approval/expansion.
+5. Human-activation boundary prevents automatic rollout activation.
+
+The first three contracts reflect live pilot state. The final two are architecture/safety contracts.
+
+## Safety closure
+- read-only certification
+- no automatic attribution
+- no automatic approval
+- no automatic expansion
+- no automatic activation
+- human commercial control preserved
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs state
+The current authoritative data has not yet established a pilot baseline, so the runtime correctly reports:
+- `V48-OPERATIONAL-WITH-OPEN-PILOT-STATE`
+- contracts currently satisfied: 2/5
+- baseline: required
+- proof: baseline required
+- executive review: baseline required
+- decision: unsigned
+- expansion plan: not authorized
+
+This does NOT mean V48 code failed certification. It means the V48 architecture is operational while the real pilot evidence workflow has not yet been executed. The synthetic full-chain certification test reaches `V48-CERTIFIED` at 5/5 contracts.
+
+## Validation
+- V48 final certification test PASS at 5/5
+- V48.20 decision-ledger regression PASS
+- V48.25 expansion-readiness regression PASS
+- authenticated V48 certification endpoint PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- automatic attribution/approval/expansion/activation all FALSE
+- npm run check PASS
+- 881 JavaScript files
+- 746 client scripts
+- 5,558 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Release status
+V48.30.0 is the planned V48 closure point. New feature work should begin in V49 rather than extending V48.
